<title>USA: Bouygues hires banker for Ciby - report.</title>
<headline>Bouygues hires banker for Ciby - report.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Construction firm Bouygues has retained French bank Societe Generale and its U.S. investment banking partner Bannon &amp; Co to find a buyer for film production company Ciby 2000, Daily Variety said Monday.</p>
<p>ICM chairman Jeff Berg was involved as an adviser, Variety said, citing sources. It said Berg declined comment and Bannon &amp; Co could not be reached for comment.</p>
<p>Bouygues was thought to be hoping to raise $75 million by selling Ciby, which has produced The Piano, Underground and Secrets &amp; Lies, Variety said.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
